course: dictionary
lesson: 430
title: Arabic: a language, a describing word, and a number sign
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word Arabic can mean three different things, and the words around it tell you which one. Look at the clues first. In «Arabic numerals», Arabic is about numbers. In «Arabic food», Arabic describes the food. A language is something people speak and read.
explain: «The Qur'an is the holy book of Islam; Muslims believe it is God's word, and it is recited in Arabic.» Here Arabic names the language the book is read in. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? If you swap in "the language" and the sentence still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
explain: «Arabic spread from Arabia across the Middle East and North Africa.» A language can spread, but a number sign cannot, so Arabic must mean the language here. Always check the sentence before you decide.
fact: Arabic is a language spoken by many millions of people in the Middle East and North Africa.
fact: Arabic is written from right to left, with its own alphabet.
fact: Arabic describes things connected with the Arabic language, Arabs and their culture, such as Arabic writing or Arabic food.
fact: Arabic numerals are the usual number signs 0, 1, 2 ... 9.
fact: Arabic numerals came to Europe through Arabic scholars, from older Indian numbers. They are different from Roman numerals such as I, V and X.
exercise: «The Qur'an is the holy book of Islam, and it is recited in Arabic.» What does Arabic mean here? | A desert | A kind of food | A number sign | *The language
exercise: In maths, which signs are called Arabic numerals? | *0, 1, 2 ... 9 | I, V, X | Up, down, left, right | A, B, C
exercise: In «Arabic food», what kind of word is Arabic? | A number sign | A verb meaning to eat | *A describing word about culture | A name for a sea
test: In «Arabic spread from Arabia across the Middle East and North Africa», what does Arabic mean? | A number | *The language | A dance | A colour
test: Which signs are Roman numerals? | a, b, c | 0, 1, 2 | 1, 2, 3, 4 | *I, V, X
exam: In «Islam is a faith in one God, called Allah in Arabic», what does Arabic mean? | A kind of food | A number sign | A place on the map | *The language
